"""Regionalized site parameters (generated by fit_regional.py on 2026-10-15; do not edit by hand).

Fitted on 268 random CONUS reference sites against Cycles v1.5.20 (continuous corn, N = 0, 150, 400 kg/ha, 37 years of tile weather and STATSGO2 soil).
For each site the net-nitrogen supply multiplier m and the grain calibration factor g that best match Cycles were found by interpolation between engine
runs, then predicted from six site covariates with small gradient-boosted trees. Out-of-fold (5-fold) these predictions cut the composite yield error 16.8%.
This is a calibration regionalization, not a mechanism: it lets the two parameters vary with site soil and climate the way pedotransfer functions let soil
properties vary with texture. Inputs are available at any CONUS location from the weather and soil tiles.
"""
